{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules","id":1218290,"title":"how to do Darth Vader King mannaseh with integrity/ Degeneration rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-13T12:05:15-07:00","id":1218290,"title":"how to do Darth Vader King mannaseh with integrity/ Degeneration rules?","content":"something Ive thought over a decade?<br /> <br /> <br /> while I know your char still has freewill regardless of his humanity/Integrity/Wisdom/Clarity/pilgrimage/Belief/Whatever<br /> <br /> but any comments on how a king mannaseh or darth vader would work in the moment of repentence in CoD?? <br /> <br /> since their score can only go up one dot at a time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T12:17:03-07:00","id":1218293,"title":"","content":"A moment of inspiration that turns a person to redeem themselves and reverse their course of sin would take them from a malicious person with low Integrity to a repentant person with low Integrity. You don't need a number on the character sheet to validate and give meaning to a transformative turning point in a person's life.<br /> <br /> Integrity measures your security of self as formed by your personal history, not how good your intentions are. Darth Vader can renounce the Dark Side and work to counteract the kind of harm he once worked on the galaxy. He's still got the scars of experience, and they will take awhile to heal until he is comfortable bearing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T14:06:47-07:00","id":1218317,"title":"","content":"integrity yes, but Humanity? <br /> <br /> And anything to say on king Mannaseh who practiced idoltry human sacrafices, etc.<br /> <br /> and was deposed taken as a prisoner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T15:06:08-07:00","id":1218335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218317#post1218317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">integrity yes, but Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity doesn\u2019t even measure altruism. It measures humanity, as in how human-like the character is. Actually this metaphor works perfectly for Darth Vader, who was \u201cmore machine now than man\u201d so would indeed have had low Humanity. There is nothing about being more man than machine that prevents him from turning back to the light side, nor does doing so magically turn his body organic. Likewise, nothing prevents a low-Humanity vampire from acting like a good person, and doing so doesn\u2019t instantly increase a vampire\u2019s Humanity.<br /> <br /> Remember, in 2e we\u2019re talking about Integrity stats, not Morality stats. They represent the well-being of the soul, not adherence to a code of ethics. Doing evil things may be damaging to the soul (or not, kinda depends on the Integrity stat in question, or in diagetic terms, the nature of the soul in question), but a damaged soul does not prevent someone from doing good things, and doing good things does not instantly repair the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T15:12:14-07:00","id":1218341,"title":"","content":"Integrity and equivalents has little bearing if any in motivations, if that's what you're asking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T15:59:51-07:00","id":1218353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218335#post1218335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity doesn\u2019t even measure altruism. It measures humanity, as in how human-like the character is. Actually this metaphor works perfectly for Darth Vader, who was \u201cmore machine now than man\u201d so would indeed have had low Humanity. There is nothing about being more man than machine that prevents him from turning back to the light side, nor does doing so magically turn his body organic. Likewise, nothing prevents a low-Humanity vampire from acting like a good person, and doing so doesn\u2019t instantly increase a vampire\u2019s Humanity.<br /> <br /> Remember, in 2e we\u2019re talking about Integrity stats, not Morality stats. They represent the well-being of the soul, not adherence to a code of ethics. Doing evil things may be damaging to the soul (or not, kinda depends on the Integrity stat in question, or in diagetic terms, the nature of the soul in question), but a damaged soul does not prevent someone from doing good things, and doing good things does not instantly repair the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> something I've thought of is that all the way to humanity 1, you may fear becoming a Draugr and try to rein in your behaviour to avoid it... that doesnt cause you to feel guilt for the people you've murdered. you just keep pushing yourself to stop killing people if you can pull it off long enough your humanity will get stronger eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T18:30:32-07:00","id":1218383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218353#post1218353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've thought of is that all the way to humanity 1, you may fear becoming a Draugr and try to rein in your behaviour to avoid it... that doesnt cause you to feel guilt for the people you've murdered. you just keep pushing yourself to stop killing people if you can pull it off long enough your humanity will get stronger eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Maybe if you're playing an anti-social character, I guess? You know there's a lot of reason to want to keep your Humanity above 0 than just avoiding becoming the draugr, right? Your Banes get worse, sunlight damage gets worse, torpor gets longer, you get worse penalties to rolls for interacting with mortals... And that's just the mechanical stuff. Whether or not your character feels guilt is entirely up to you as a player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T00:31:30-07:00","id":1218433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218317#post1218317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And anything to say on king Mannaseh who practiced idoltry human sacrafices, etc.<br /> and was deposed taken as a prisoner.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a character from scripture. He's not exactly a nuanced character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T05:14:46-07:00","id":1218479,"title":"","content":"Another good/interesting take on a low Humanity vampire would be Dracula from the Netflix Castlevania series (and the character in the tangled Castlevania source material). He's pretty &quot;low Humanity&quot; regardless, in that he doesn't really identify as human. Before &quot;the incident&quot;, he appears to be <i>trying</i> to increase his Humanity a bit, but it is obviously still low. It... doesn't really look to improve much from there. (Trying to avoid spoilers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:54:56-07:00","id":1218614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218383#post1218383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Maybe if you're playing an anti-social character, I guess? You know there's a lot of reason to want to keep your Humanity above 0 than just avoiding becoming the draugr, right? Your Banes get worse, sunlight damage gets worse, torpor gets longer, you get worse penalties to rolls for interacting with mortals... And that's just the mechanical stuff. Whether or not your character feels guilt is entirely up to you as a player.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> cant majesty or dominate substite for most of those problems? <br /> <br /> a weird observation of mine but one that rings true. that while relying on such powers can knock you off the higher rank's of humanity... they can help stabilize moderate humanity, by making murder much less tempting? <br /> <br /> But even for a daeva im sure theirs reasons not to dismiss The social penaltys from 1 dot of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:06:05-07:00","id":1218617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218614#post1218614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cant majesty or dominate substite for most of those problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. They can help with precisely <i>one</i> of those problems - the penalty to mundane social rolls with mortals. They will do nothing to alleviate your Banes, help you avoid the sun, or wake you up from torpor faster. They also tend to cost Vitae to make people do what you want, so it\u2019s not a real solution, it\u2019s a workaround that costs a limited resource.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218614#post1218614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a weird observation of mine but one that rings true. that while relying on such powers can knock you off the higher rank's of humanity... they can help stabilize moderate humanity, by making murder much less tempting?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s true that Discipline use can help stabilize Humanity at mid-levels, yes. I\u2019m not understanding what temptation to murder has to do with it. Anyway, if you expect your character to lose a lot of Humanity due to murder, just take a Bane for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218290-how-to-do-darth-vader-king-mannaseh-with-integrity-degeneration-rules?p=1218614#post1218614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even for a daeva im sure theirs reasons not to dismiss The social penaltys from 1 dot of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because you won\u2019t always want to rely on Majesty when interacting with mortals.<br /> <br /> What was your point again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}